! Floating-point diagnostic jb_af1c, routine F211 "STORE LOW ORDER
! TEST ROUTINE", "TEST NORMALIZATION MODIFIER", sub-tests A7-A10
! (docs/jb_af1c_floating-point.pdf p.114, octal 016217.00-016243.00,
! the routine's own exit "BD,$+1.0"). Twenty-eight rows, closing
! F211A.
!
! The first SLO(N) anywhere, and between them these four cover every
! part of SLO the earlier sub-tests could not reach. A1-A6 are all
! SLO(U).
!
!   A7  FK23 (XFP +1023) with FK26's fraction in the low half. The
!       accumulator exponent is FLAGGED, so p.97 says normalization is
!       suppressed -- and FK26 is the expected result, still
!       unnormalized (155555555555, three leading zeros). Asking for
!       (N) must change nothing.
!   A8  the same in XFN with FK25 and FK30 (1fffffffffff).
!   A9  the real normalization. FPK37 is exponent +50; FPK53's
!       fraction is 000000000002 -- a single bit near the bottom, 46
!       leading zeros. SLO(N) subtracts 48 to get +2, then shifts left
!       46 places to 800000000000, taking the exponent to -44.
!       Expected FK51: exponent -44, fraction 800000000000. The
!       listing says so: "CHECK RESULT WITH EXP+-44".
!   A10 the GENERATED flag. FK111 is exponent -1023; FK88's fraction
!       normalizes two places; so the exponent goes -1023 - 48 - 2 =
!       -1073, which is out of range. p.97: "When the exponent with
!       the low order fraction has EF of 1 as a result of the
!       operation, the indicator settings are for generated exponent
!       flags. Normalization, if specified, in this case DOES occur."
!       The listing's own comment is "GENERATED EXP FLAG".
!
! A10 CAUGHT A REAL MODEL BUG, and the prediction written here before
! the run was borne out exactly. FK112 is XFN with exponent field -49,
! and 1073 - 1024 = 49: the machine keeps the LOW TEN BITS of an
! out-of-range magnitude in the exponent field and uses EF only to
! mark that it overflowed. fpMakeExp instead wrote em = 0 whenever it
! generated a flag --
!
!     Bit#(10) em = gen ? 10'd0 : truncate(pack(mag));
!
! -- so the model stored XFN -0 where the listing wants XFN -49. A10
! halted on its CT0110 with SIC storing 016243.00, and A7, A8 and A9
! all passed, A9 being the control: it normalizes too, but stays in
! range and so never reaches the clamp. The fix is to drop the
! conditional and always keep the low ten bits.
!
! The bug is in code much older than SLO. fpMakeExp is shared by
! fpAdd, fpAddDouble, SRD and SLO, and every exponent any of them
! builds goes through it. Nothing in the suite had pinned it, because
! nothing before A10 drove an exponent out of range and then LOOKED at
! the field rather than just at EF. The full suite stays green with
! the fix, so nothing had been written against the wrong behaviour
! either.
!
! ROS (022355) is the routine's scratch word, not a pool constant.
! Framework substitutes as everywhere else in this series: SERS (octal
! 1304) -> FAIL halt, SEN (octal 1310) -> scratch. Constants from the
! pools pp.176-179. PASS sits at 016243.00, on the routine's exit.
!
! Instructions: DL(U), C0011, SLO(N), L, CT0110, SIC, BRGZ.
! verify_fp_arith_f211a7_10_listing.py checks every word bit-for-bit.

! -- SSIP framework substitutes --
        SLC, (8)1304.0
SERS    BEW, $
        SLC, (8)1310.0
SEN     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- the routine's scratch word --
        SLC, (8)22355.0
ROS     DD(BU,64,8), 0

! -- constants (pools pp.176-179) --
        SLC, (8)022052.0
FPK37   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0031125252525252525240
        SLC, (8)022072.0
FPK53   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0000400000000000000040
        SLC, (8)022171.0
FK23    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777525252525252525240
        SLC, (8)22173.0
FK25    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1577777777777777777760
FK26    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1777412525252525252520
        SLC, (8)022200.0
FK30    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1577617777777777777760
        SLC, (8)022225.0
FK51    DD(BU,64,8), (8)0026300000000000000000
        SLC, (8)022271.0
FK88    DD(BU,64,8), (8)1577624713560247135620
        SLC, (8)022320.0
FK111   DD(BU,64,8), (8)0777625777252525777250
FK112   DD(BU,64,8), (8)1030723456701234567100

! The listing prints no label at 016217.00 -- ENTRY is ours, needed
! only as the END operand.
! -- code (verbatim, at the listing's addresses) --
        SLC, (8)16217.0
ENTRY   DL(U), FK23                            ! F211A7: exp in XFP rng
        C0011(BU,48), FK26+.12, 20
        SLO(N), ROS
        L(BU), FK26
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 4
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        DL(U), FK25                            ! F211A8: exp in XFN rng
        C0011(BU,48), FK30+.12, 20
        SLO(N), ROS
        L(BU), FK30
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 4
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        DL(U), FPK37                           ! F211A9: exp + +50, N rng
        C0011(BU,48), FPK53+.12, 20
        SLO(N), ROS
        L(BU), FK51
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 4                  ! check result with exp + -44
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
        DL(U), FK111                           ! F211A10: exp + -1023, N rng
        C0011(BU,48), FK88+.12, 20
        SLO(N), ROS
        L(BU), FK112
        CT0110(BU,60), ROS, 4                  ! generated exp flag
        SIC, SEN
        BRGZ, SERS
PASS    BEW, $                                 ! 016243.00: the routine's exit ("BD,$+1.0")
        END, ENTRY
